perf(pip): Finish the log audit: the upscaler and reset lines were repeating once per aim

A full sweep for log writes on our paths, beyond the probes already switched off, found the last
repeaters: the upscaler re-initialises every time the scope resolution override toggles, which is
once per aim, and each re-init wrote its own lines.

 - "[DLSS] Initialized; awaiting first scene evaluation" (or the FSR3 equivalent) is now written once
   per session, not on every rebuild. The first line carries all of it.
 - "- [DLSS] ACTIVE - first scene evaluation succeeded" likewise, once per session.
 - the "STOPPED - using spatial upscale" error was written every frame while a failure lasted; it is
   now reported once per failure episode (the error state for the UI is still updated every frame).
 - "* [RESET/RENDER TARGET] ..." is written on the first reset and then only at r__svp_debug 1, since
   later resets are the override toggling once per aim rather than anything the player needs to see.

What the audit leaves in a normal session: the per session lines (build stamp, pack policy, target
set created, the upscaler's first lines), one line per aim (the aim summary, the thermal optic line,
and the state line when it changes) and the five minute heartbeats. Everything else we added - the
content probes, the readbacks, the image dumps, the per pass lines - is behind r__svp_debug and off
by default. render_stats::Publish writes nothing to the log at all; it only feeds the stats overlay.